    console.log("No matching PIN found.");
}
```

In this example, the script iterates through all 4-digit numbers from 1000 to 9999, checks if the current number is the target PIN (2588 in this case), and stores the found PIN in an array. If a match is found, it logs the PIN to the console.

However, it's important to note that brute-forcing can be computationally expensive and time-consuming, especially for larger solution spaces. It's also not always the most efficient or practical method, as there are often more efficient algorithms available for solving problems. Always consider the complexity of the problem and the available resources before deciding to use brute-forcing.

